WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.888
DNS Firewall applies rule groups
of allow, alert and block rules.

2
00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:10.988
It uses custom or AWS managed domain lists,
and the managed lists can't be browsed.

3
00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:16.438
The Advanced tier detects domain
generation algorithms and DNS tunneling.

4
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:21.187
It filters only queries that pass
through the VPC Resolver, including those

5
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:26.313
arriving through inbound endpoints, and by
default it fails closed, with SERVFAIL.

6
00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:31.247
Query logging records queries from
the VPC, through the endpoints,

7
00:00:31.247 --> 00:00:35.374
and firewall actions, to
CloudWatch Logs, S3 or Firehose.

8
00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:40.675
It logs only queries that reach the VPC
Resolver, and not answers from its cache.

9
00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:46.450
DNSSEC: the VPC Resolver can validate
public signed names, enabled per VPC.

10
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.650
Route 53 signs public hosted zones only.

11
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.958
And the VPC Resolver
returns no DNSSEC records,

12
00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:56.350
so a resolver behind it
can't validate for itself.

13
00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.740
AWS warns that enabling validation
could result in an outage.
